Fork note: backported onto Servo v0.6.0 for the ohos-v0.6 branch without its Cargo.lock change, as the mozjs update before it already takes encoding_rs from 0.8.35 to 0.8.44. What is left is the expectation file it deletes: encoding_rs 0.8.40 fixed buffer boundaries in streaming two-byte legacy decoders, so the big5, euc-kr and shift_jis stream subtests of textdecoder-mistakes pass now.

Validation: On the final stack, at its tip: `./mach test-tidy` (including cargo-deny), `./mach test-scripts`, `./mach clippy --locked -- -- --deny warnings`, the crown build (checked-release, -D warnings, crown built for Rust 1.97.1), `./mach test-unit --profile checked-release` with and without `--doc`, and the OpenHarmony checked-release builds of both flavors with -D warnings, which make signed HAPs, pass; release builds of it with both engines ran the whole WPT suite. textdecoder-mistakes.any.html and .any.worker.html run as expected with both engines in the stack's full runs. On this branch's first version, which also carried the ArkWeb port and the other patches it leaves out now, the three stream subtests passed in all 27 runs after the mozjs update (17 with SpiderMonkey, 10 with QuickJS), and plain v0.6.0 failed them in all of its 8.
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; the agent took upstream commit 00a278f26a9 without its Cargo.lock change and added the fork-style part of this message below the dashed line: fork note, Validation and these trailers)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
